{
  "$comment": [
    "Deterministic emergency detection. Runs BEFORE any model call, on every",
    "inbound message, on every surface.",
    "",
    "WHY NOT LET THE MODEL DECIDE: a model judging whether chest pain is urgent is",
    "right almost always. 'Almost always' is an acceptable bar for choosing a tone",
    "and an unacceptable one for choosing whether someone is told to call an",
    "ambulance. Rules run first; the model only ever confirms.",
    "",
    "BIAS: deliberately toward false positives. Wrongly telling a well person to",
    "seek urgent care costs them an inconvenience. Wrongly telling an unwell person",
    "to book a clinic appointment costs something that cannot be refunded.",
    "",
    "MATCHING: normalised Arabic (alef/hamza folded, tatweel and diacritics",
    "stripped). Egyptian colloquial first — patients do not write 'ضيق في التنفس',",
    "they write 'مش لاقي نفسي'.",
    "",
    "  terms[]         — substring match.",
    "  cooccurrence[]  — every fragment must appear somewhere in the message, in",
    "                    any order. This is how Arabic conjugation is handled:",
    "                    ['مش قادر','تنفس'] catches 'مش قادر أتنفس', 'مش قادرة",
    "                    تتنفس', 'مش قادر يتنفس' and 'امي مش قادرة خالص تتنفس'",
    "                    with one rule. A fixed term list cannot cover the",
    "                    conjugations, and the gap is invisible until a real",
    "                    patient hits it — this one was found by a test, not in",
    "                    production, which is the whole point of having the test.",
    "",
    "⚠️ REVIEW: this file must be reviewed by the clinician named in",
    "receptionist/docs/NEEDS_OPERATOR.md §7 before any live channel is opened.",
    "It has not been reviewed yet."
  ],
